name issue_453_sps_pps_tracker_high_jitter
describe high_jitter with the receiver's H.264 SPS/PPS tracker on: an IDR start that arrives before its SPS and PPS is dropped and a keyframe requested, as libwebrtc (issue #453)
# libwebrtc's RtpVideoStreamReceiver2::OnReceivedPayloadData runs H264SpsPpsTracker::CopyAndFixBitstream on every
# H.264 packet (video/rtp_video_stream_receiver2.cc, kRequestKeyframe -> RequestKeyFrame + kIgnore). With 40 ms jitter
# and reordering, the first keyframe's IDR start overtakes its SPS+PPS STAP-A on seed 1, so libwebrtc decodes the
# second keyframe instead: time to first frame 665 ms, 2 keyframe requests (parity-data, compare-webrtc.json).
# Seed 1: tracker off 200 ms / 0 requests; on 740 ms / 2 requests. The packet buffer's H.264 hold is turned off
# here so the scenario keeps measuring the tracker alone (issue_453_h264_missing_packets_high_jitter has both).
# 10 seeds (1-10), ours off / on / libwebrtc: time to first frame 228 / 449 / 433 ms; keyframe requests 0.4 / 1.7 / 1.2.
duration 30s
seed 1
sps_pps_tracker on
h264_missing_packets off
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=30ms jitter=40ms reorder=on queue=300ms
expect video.time_to_first_frame_ms > 600
expect video.keyframe_requests >= 2
expect audio.interruptions == 0
expect audio.concealed_pct < 2
